                                    <p>Fragment of marble relief broken at top and both sides; there was apparently a lug at the bottom for insertion into a base. Height 16 cm., width 16.3 cm., thickness 3.7 cm. Found in the excavations of the Athenian Agora, April 15, 1936, and now in the Agora Museum.</p>
